---@class aws.neptunedata.GetSparqlStreamInput
---@field limit? number Specifies the maximum number of records to return. There is also a size limit of 10 MB on the response that can't be modified and that takes precedence over the number of records specified in the limit parameter. The response does include a threshold-breaching record if the 10 MB limit was reached.
---@field iteratorType? aws.neptunedata.IteratorType|string Can be one of:
---@field commitNum? number The commit number of the starting record to read from the change-log stream. This parameter is required when iteratorType isAT_SEQUENCE_NUMBER or AFTER_SEQUENCE_NUMBER, and ignored when iteratorType is TRIM_HORIZON or LATEST.
---@field opNum? number The operation sequence number within the specified commit to start reading from in the change-log stream data. The default is 1.
---@field encoding? aws.neptunedata.Encoding|string If set to TRUE, Neptune compresses the response using gzip encoding.

---@class aws.neptunedata.GetSparqlStreamOutput
---@field lastEventId aws.neptunedata.StringValuedMap Sequence identifier of the last change in the stream response.
---@field lastTrxTimestampInMillis number The time at which the commit for the transaction was requested, in milliseconds from the Unix epoch.
---@field format string Serialization format for the change records being returned. Currently, the only supported value is NQUADS.
---@field records aws.neptunedata.SparqlRecordsList An array of serialized change-log stream records included in the response.
---@field totalRecords number The total number of records in the response.

